<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech import depos to be accepted by all banks-CTK.</title>
<headline>Czech import depos to be accepted by all banks-CTK.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>All Czech banks, not just five as originally planned, will be allowed to collect import deposits, the CTK news agency quoted Industry and Trade Minister Vladimir Dlouhy as saying on Monday.</p>
<p>The import deposit plan, announced last week as part of a government plan to reverse the trend of a widening trade deficit, took effect on Monday.</p>
<p>Under the deposit scheme, importers will be required to deposit 20 percent of the value of imported consumer goods on an interest-free account for 180 days.</p>
<p>The original plan included only five banks -- Komercni Banka, Ceskoslovenska Obchodni Banka, Ceska Sporitelna, IPB, and Union Banka.</p>
<p>But many other banks, as well as the central bank, protested the move saying it was unfair.</p>
<p>-- Jan Lopatka, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
